		"nodes": {
			"19": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": true
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "ABSOLUTE\nThe Absolute node calculates the absolute value of the given input. Basically this means that any negative input is made positive.\n\nExample A: -2 becomes 2.\nExample B:  5 becomes 5.\n\nThe following patch contains all the basic rounding functions in Wire.\nUse the slider to adjust the value that is to be rounded.\nThe height of the red rectangle is directly modulated by the value slider.\nThe height of the yellow rectangle is modulated by the absolute value.\n\nPatch Explained -\n\n• The slider provides a value between -5 and 5 to the rounding nodes. The Join node combines their values in an array so we can adres each instance of the rectangle in the Transform node.\n"
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 358,
					"width": 811,
					"x": 280.5999755859375,
					"y": -53
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
